{"name":"High Tide","hex":"#85a6c8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"high tide","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The natural tide at its highest level for a particular tidal cycle at a certain place.","The time of day when the sea has risen to its highest level."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative form of high-tide."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/high_tide"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tide","blocks":[{"text":"Tides are the periodic rise and fall of sea level resulting from the differential gravitational forces exerted primarily by the Moon and the Sun, combined with inertial effects associated with the Earth–Moon system’s orbital motion and the Earth's rotation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Tide_overview.svg/330px-Tide_overview.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tide","wikidata":"Q23384"},{"title":"High Tide (1947 film)","blocks":[{"text":"High Tide is a 1947 American film noir directed by John Reinhardt. The film features Lee Tracy, Don Castle and Julie Bishop."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/42/High_tide_1947_poster_small.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/High_Tide_(1947_film)","wikidata":"Q3613082"},{"title":"High Tide (band)","blocks":[{"text":"High Tide were an English rock band formed in 1969 by Tony Hill, Simon House, Peter Pavli and Roger Hadden (drums). They released two studio albums under their own name for Liberty Records and one as backing musicians for Denny Gerrard. They broke up in 1970 after little critical or commercial success.\nTony Hill's vocals/vocal stylings are strongly reminiscent of The Doors' Jim Morrison."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/High_Tide_(band)","wikidata":"Q943582"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Tide_and_Moon.jpg/330px-Tide_and_Moon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Tide_and_Moon.jpg/330px-Tide_and_Moon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"In Maine (U.S.), low tide occurs roughly at moonrise and high tide with a high Moon, corresponding to the simple gravity model of two tidal bulges; at most places however, the Moon and tides have a phase shift.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATide_and_Moon.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Tide_terms.png/500px-Tide_terms.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Tide_terms.png/500px-Tide_terms.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Illustration by the course of half a month","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATide_terms.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/High_tide_sun_moon_same_side_beginning.png/120px-High_tide_sun_moon_same_side_beginning.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/High_tide_sun_moon_same_side_beginning.png/250px-High_tide_sun_moon_same_side_beginning.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/High_tide_sun_moon_same_side_beginning.png/120px-High_tide_sun_moon_same_side_beginning.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHigh_tide_sun_moon_same_side_beginning.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Low_tide_sun_moon_90_degrees.png/120px-Low_tide_sun_moon_90_degrees.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.o